From: Hermes Patches <patches@local>
Subject: [PATCH] fix(runtime): separate OpenRouter key routing and retry 516 anomalies

OpenRouter requests must use OPENROUTER_API_KEY, not a generic
OPENAI_API_KEY. This prevents auto/runtime paths from sending a custom
OpenAI-compatible key to https://openrouter.ai/api/v1 and receiving a
misleading 401.

Also adds the chat-completions 516 anomaly guard and route-targeted live
canary. The guard treats a known-bad reasoning-only 200 response with
reasoning_tokens=516, no visible content, and no tool calls as a synthetic
retryable 502 so the existing retry/fallback path handles it.

Verification:
- python -m pytest -q -o addopts='' tests/hermes_cli/test_openrouter_key_routing.py tests/run_agent/test_chat_completions_516_anomaly_live.py
- python -m pytest -q -o addopts='' tests/run_agent/test_516_anomaly_guard.py tests/hermes_cli/test_runtime_provider_resolution.py
- python -m pytest -q -o addopts='' tests/run_agent/test_516_anomaly_guard.py tests/hermes_cli/test_openrouter_key_routing.py tests/hermes_cli/test_runtime_provider_resolution.py tests/run_agent/test_chat_completions_516_anomaly_live.py

